    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d319">

                <pb facs="0300" n="290" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg290"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.002/2–2549: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Taipei</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Krentz</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Taipei</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-02-25T17:00:00+08:00">February 25,
                            1949—5 p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 9:04 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>52. Chen Cheng is now governing by a kitchen cabinet of generals, notably Lo
                    Cho-ying, with nominal department heads ineffective, frustrated while
                    deterioration all fields visible daily.</p>
                <p>Repeated Embassy 45.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Krentz</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
